INSERT INTO `candidate_profiles` VALUES (1,'gemini-2.5-flash-lite','cv-parse-v1','2026-10-01 03:42:37.330844',NULL,'SUCCESS','2026-10-01 03:42:37.327843','NGUYỄN VĂN DŨNG \nJUNIOR JAVA BACKEND DEVELOPER \n \nContact Information: \n- Phone: (+84) 912 345 678 \n- Email: nguyenvananh.dev@gmail.com \n- Location: Cau Giay District, Hanoi, Vietnam \n- LinkedIn: linkedin.com/in/nguyen-van-anh-java \n- GitHub: github.com/nguyenvananh-dev \n \n-------------------------------------------------- \nOBJECTIVE \n-------------------------------------------------- \nDetail-oriented and motivated Junior Java Backend Developer based in Hanoi with strong \nhands-on experience in the Spring Boot ecosystem, microservices patterns, caching, and \ndatabase optimization. Eager to contribute to scalable, high-performance web applications at \na dynamic technology company while continuously expanding technical expertise. \n \n-------------------------------------------------- \nEDUCATION \n-------------------------------------------------- \nBachelor of Science in Software Engineering \nHanoi University of Science and Technology (HUST) / (Transfer/Study equivalent based in \nHanoi) \n2022 - Present (Expected Graduation: June 2026) \n- GPA: 3.4 / 4.0 \n- Relevant Coursework: Data Structures & Algorithms, Object-Oriented Programming, \nDatabase Systems, Computer Networks, Software Architecture. \n \n-------------------------------------------------- \nWORK EXPERIENCE \n-------------------------------------------------- \n1. FPT Software - Junior Java Backend Developer \n   - Timeframe: 07/2025 - 01/2026 | Location: Hanoi, Vietnam \n   - Description: A leading global IT services and software outsourcing provider delivering \nenterprise solutions for international clients. \n   - Key Responsibilities & Achievements: \n     * Developed and maintained core RESTful APIs using Spring Boot and Spring Data JPA \nfor a large-scale enterprise logistics platform, handling over 50,000 daily active requests. \n     * Integrated Redis for distributed caching of frequent lookup data, reducing database \nquery load by 35% and improving response times. \n     * Collaborated with senior engineers to refactor monolith modules into lightweight \nmicroservices, using RabbitMQ for reliable asynchronous event-driven communication. \n     * Wrote comprehensive unit and integration tests using JUnit 5 and Mockito, increasing \ncode test coverage from 60% to over 80%. \n     * Participated in Daily Standups, Code Reviews, and sprint planning following \nAgile/Scrum methodologies. \n\n\n\n \n2. Viettel Solutions - Java Backend Intern / Fresher \n   - Timeframe: 11/2024 - 05/2025 | Location: Hanoi, Vietnam \n   - Description: A major digital transformation partner and technology solutions provider \nunder Viettel Group. \n   - Key Responsibilities & Achievements: \n     * Assisted in designing and implementing secure user authentication and authorization \nmodules using Spring Security and JWT. \n     * Optimized PostgreSQL database queries and created complex indexing strategies, \nresolving slow-running query bottlenecks on high-volume reporting tables. \n     * Configured Docker containers and wrote Dockerfiles for multi-tier microservices \napplications to ensure consistency across development, staging, and production \nenvironments. \n     * Maintained CI/CD pipelines using GitHub Actions to automate building, testing, and \ndeployment processes. \n \n3. VNEXT Software - Software Engineering Intern \n   - Timeframe: 06/2024 - 10/2024 | Location: Hanoi, Vietnam \n   - Description: A professional software development company specializing in web and \nmobile applications for Japanese and global markets. \n   - Key Responsibilities & Achievements: \n     * Built reusable backend components and integrated third-party REST APIs (payment \ngateways, notification services) into core SaaS products. \n     * Utilized Git/GitHub for version control, resolving merge conflicts, and participating in \npeer code review workflows. \n     * Monitored server health, analyzed application logs via ELK stack basics, and assisted in \ntroubleshooting production bugs under the guidance of senior mentors. \n \n \n-------------------------------------------------- \nSKILLS \n-------------------------------------------------- \n- Programming Languages: Java (8/17/21), JavaScript, HTML/CSS \n- Frameworks & Libraries: Spring Boot, Spring Data JPA, Spring Security, Spring Cloud \n(Basic), ReactJS \n- Databases & Caching: MySQL, PostgreSQL, Redis \n- DevOps & Tools: Git/GitHub, Docker, Nginx, Postman, Maven, Gradle, Linux CLI \n- Architecture & Messaging: RESTful APIs, Microservices concepts, RabbitMQ, Spring AI, \nJWT, VNPay Sandbox, WebSocket \n \n-------------------------------------------------- \nPROJECTS \n-------------------------------------------------- \n1. Tour Booking System \n   - Timeframe: 01/2026 - Present | Role: Fullstack Developer (Solo Project) \n   - Description: A high-performance tour booking and recommendation platform designed for \nseamless user experience and secure transactions. \n   - Key Responsibilities & Achievements: \n\n\n\n     * Engineered an intelligent RAG-based Chatbot using Spring AI and PostgreSQL \n(pgvector) with HNSW indexing, delivering personalized tour recommendations and direct \nbooking navigation. \n     * Implemented safe tour booking using Redis-based distributed locks to prevent race \nconditions and double-booking, ensuring strict data consistency under concurrent user \naccess. \n     * Integrated RabbitMQ for asynchronous processing of booking confirmations and \npayment receipts via email, significantly reducing API response latency. \n     * Optimized page load performance leveraging Redis caching and integrated VNPay \nSandbox for secure, real-time online financial transactions. \n     * Deployed the production-ready system to Digital Ocean using Docker for \ncontainerization, configuring Nginx as a Reverse Proxy and Load Balancer. \n   - Links: Live Demo (Hosted) | GitHub: github.com/nguyenvananh-dev/tour-booking-system \n \n2. Social Network Application \n   - Timeframe: 02/2025 - 05/2025 | Role: Backend Developer (Team Size: 4) \n   - Description: A collaborative social platform providing dynamic posting, real-time \nmessaging, and interactive social feeds. \n   - Key Responsibilities & Achievements: \n     * Designed and developed robust RESTful APIs to support core platform functionalities, \nincluding user profiles, dynamic posts, comments, and friend management workflows. \n     * Implemented secure authentication and authorization using Spring Security and JWT, \nfeaturing strict Role-Based Access Control (RBAC) for User and Admin privileges. \n     * Integrated Cloudinary for scalable, cloud-based media uploading and persistent \nimage/video storage. \n     * Built responsive frontend components using ReactJS and established seamless \nclient-server communication. \n     * Implemented real-time notifications for user interactions (likes, comments, friend \nrequests) using Spring WebSocket and STOMP protocol, integrated with a custom JWT \nInterceptor for secure handshakes. \n   - Links: GitHub (Backend): github.com/nguyenvananh-dev/social-network-backend | \nGitHub (Frontend): github.com/nguyenvananh-dev/social-network-frontend \n \n-------------------------------------------------- \nCERTIFICATES \n-------------------------------------------------- \n- TOEIC 615 (Reading & Listening) \n  * Issued: 03/2026 \n  * Proficient in reading technical documentation, writing code comments, and collaborating \nin English-speaking work environments.','Detail-oriented and motivated Junior Java Backend Developer based in Hanoi with strong hands-on experience in the Spring Boot ecosystem, microservices patterns, caching, and database optimization. Eager to contribute to scalable, high-performance web applications at a dynamic technology company while continuously expanding technical expertise.',1.3,'2026-10-01 03:42:37.330844',6);
